1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,560
The second day began before the sun. The radio was still tuned to 87.0.

2
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:15,320
Between bursts of static I heard it again. Block 17. Then three short knocks. I waited for an

3
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:21,880
explanation. Only the hiss of static followed. Outside, screams cut across the street. A bus

4
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:25,720
was burning at the intersection and people were running, not knowing where to hide.

5
00:00:26,255 --> 00:00:30,695
The bandage on my arm was damp. I replaced the fabric without looking too

6
00:00:30,695 --> 00:00:33,975
closely at the mark. It hadn't disappeared but it didn't seem any

7
00:00:33,975 --> 00:00:38,375
larger either. That brought me no comfort. On the first night I had learned

8
00:00:38,375 --> 00:00:42,149
that being on one's feet and being fine were two very different things.

9
00:00:42,149 --> 00:00:45,069
The older woman was already awake in the hallway.

10
00:00:45,069 --> 00:00:49,029
When I mentioned the radio, she glanced toward the stairwell door.

11
00:00:49,029 --> 00:00:50,589
She didn't want to come along.

12
00:00:50,589 --> 00:00:54,029
She said she knew this building better than the streets outside.

13
00:00:54,029 --> 00:00:58,269
I left her some water, agreed on a signal of two knocks for when I returned, and promised

14
00:00:58,269 --> 00:01:01,022
not to turn hope into just another locked door.

15
00:01:01,022 --> 00:01:05,022
The maintenance worker appeared, carrying a ring of keys.

16
00:01:05,022 --> 00:01:07,022
He had heard the same broadcast.

17
00:01:07,022 --> 00:01:09,462
"Block 17," he repeated.

18
00:01:09,462 --> 00:01:11,622
He pointed toward the school across the street.

19
00:01:11,622 --> 00:01:14,262
There was a service entrance beneath the courtyard.

20
00:01:14,262 --> 00:01:15,942
He knew how to open the first door.

21
00:01:15,942 --> 00:01:18,102
As for the second one, I knew nothing more.

22
00:01:18,806 --> 00:01:23,566
We set out just as the light began to touch the windows. The noise from the day before

23
00:01:23,566 --> 00:01:29,966
persisted. Sirens, shattering glass, people calling out for those left behind. A crowd

24
00:01:29,966 --> 00:01:34,486
came running down the road. We walked close to the walls, trying not to get swept up in

25
00:01:34,486 --> 00:01:42,736
the rush. A car was blocking the corner. Behind it, someone stood motionless, back turned, listening to something.

26
00:01:42,736 --> 00:01:48,096
The worker stepped on a shard of glass. It was a faint sound, but the man's head snapped

27
00:01:48,096 --> 00:01:53,576
around instantly. I pulled my companion behind the car. Others emerged from between

28
00:01:53,576 --> 00:01:58,176
the buses, chasing a group that had broken through the evacuation barrier. None of them

29
00:01:58,176 --> 00:02:03,016
were searching with their eyes. They all stopped, tilted their heads, and waited for

30
00:02:03,016 --> 00:02:03,816
another sound.

31
00:02:04,215 --> 00:02:07,335
A car slammed into the side of an ambulance.

32
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:11,095
The alarm went off and the infected rushed toward the crash while two survivors tried

33
00:02:11,095 --> 00:02:12,855
to climb out the window.

34
00:02:12,855 --> 00:02:15,635
We seized the opening and crossed without a word.

35
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,975
My arm hit the fence and the pain made me stumble.

36
00:02:18,975 --> 00:02:21,095
The worker grabbed me by the coat.

37
00:02:21,095 --> 00:02:24,415
For the first time since it all began, someone turned back to help me.

38
00:02:24,775 --> 00:02:28,015
The school gate was open just wide enough for one person.

39
00:02:28,015 --> 00:02:32,135
In the courtyard, backpacks lay scattered beside overturned chairs.

40
00:02:32,135 --> 00:02:37,015
Behind the fence, people were pushing against the gate, while an infected individual advanced

41
00:02:37,015 --> 00:02:38,015
through the line.

42
00:02:38,015 --> 00:02:40,695
There was no one left waiting for rescue.

43
00:02:40,695 --> 00:02:43,895
The service door was located behind the electrical box.

44
00:02:43,895 --> 00:02:47,655
The key slid in, turned, and made a noise that sounded deafening.

45
00:02:47,951 --> 00:02:52,151
Before we could head down, a flashlight cut across the hallway.

46
00:02:52,151 --> 00:02:54,551
The officer ordered us to show our hands.

47
00:02:54,551 --> 00:02:59,311
I recognized the uniform, the same one I'd seen near the evacuation zone.

48
00:02:59,311 --> 00:03:03,191
He glanced at my bandage but didn't ask what had happened.

49
00:03:03,191 --> 00:03:05,591
Instead he asked if we had the radio.

50
00:03:05,591 --> 00:03:07,391
When I said yes, he lowered the light.

51
00:03:07,774 --> 00:03:10,454
He too was looking for Block 17.

52
00:03:10,454 --> 00:03:12,774
He had found a record with that designation,

53
00:03:12,774 --> 00:03:15,774
filed four days before everything came to a halt.

54
00:03:15,774 --> 00:03:19,774
The man spread out an old blueprint of the school on a table.

55
00:03:19,774 --> 00:03:22,774
It showed a passageway beneath the sports court.

56
00:03:22,774 --> 00:03:24,174
Three people.

57
00:03:24,174 --> 00:03:26,774
Three fragments of the same story.

58
00:03:26,774 --> 00:03:28,774
None of them held the complete answer.

59
00:03:28,964 --> 00:03:30,964
We descended slowly.

60
00:03:30,964 --> 00:03:35,964
The officer’s light swept over pipes, puddles, and handprints on the walls.

61
00:03:35,964 --> 00:03:39,964
Down here, the sounds from the street grew muffled.

62
00:03:39,964 --> 00:03:42,964
I could hear the trickle of water in the sound of our own breathing.

63
00:03:42,964 --> 00:03:45,964
The radio crackled inside the backpack.

64
00:03:45,964 --> 00:03:48,964
I grabbed the volume knob before it could draw any attention.

65
00:03:49,137 --> 00:03:54,137
Around the final bend a door appeared, marked with the number 17.

66
00:03:54,137 --> 00:03:56,137
From the other side came two knocks.

67
00:03:56,137 --> 00:04:01,137
I nearly responded with the signal I'd agreed upon back at the building, but the officer caught my wrist.

68
00:04:01,137 --> 00:04:02,137
We waited.

69
00:04:02,137 --> 00:04:06,137
The same two knocks came again, with the exact same interval.

70
00:04:06,137 --> 00:04:09,962
Whatever was on the other side wasn't responding to anyone.

71
00:04:09,962 --> 00:04:13,022
I turned the radio volume down low.

72
00:04:13,022 --> 00:04:15,182
The voice came through more clearly.

73
00:04:15,182 --> 00:04:17,582
Do not use the main entrance.

74
00:04:17,582 --> 00:04:19,462
The message repeated.

75
00:04:19,462 --> 00:04:22,862
This time I understood why the address stood alone amidst the static.

76
00:04:22,862 --> 00:04:25,102
It wasn't a promise of rescue.

77
00:04:25,102 --> 00:04:29,102
It was a warning that someone was trying to keep alive, even without being able to

78
00:04:29,102 --> 00:04:29,942
explain why.

79
00:04:30,336 --> 00:04:34,216
The side passage had a metal gate with a jammed latch.

80
00:04:34,216 --> 00:04:37,615
The employee wrapped a cloth around the metal before forcing it.

81
00:04:37,615 --> 00:04:40,495
The police officer kept his flashlight pointed toward the bend.

82
00:04:40,496 --> 00:04:43,456
I held the gate to keep it from falling.

83
00:04:43,456 --> 00:04:48,576
When the latch finally gave way, the three of us remained perfectly still, listening

84
00:04:48,576 --> 00:04:49,776
to see if anything had changed.

85
00:04:50,150 --> 00:04:52,550
Behind the gate was a utility room.

86
00:04:52,550 --> 00:04:56,650
Batteries, papers, and an old receiver cluttered the tables.

87
00:04:56,650 --> 00:04:59,150
The log for Block 17 was in a drawer,

88
00:04:59,150 --> 00:05:01,150
along with some handwritten schedules.

89
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:03,150
Dated four days prior.

90
00:05:03,150 --> 00:05:05,150
The date made no sense to me.

91
00:05:05,150 --> 00:05:07,150
But the paper was there.

92
00:05:07,150 --> 00:05:10,150
Someone had been listening before us.

93
00:05:10,614 --> 00:05:14,214
On the back of one sheet, I found a name.

94
00:05:14,214 --> 00:05:15,214
Rosa.

95
00:05:15,214 --> 00:05:20,634
It was just a small signature, next to a transmission test.

96
00:05:20,634 --> 00:05:23,414
My phone still had no signal.

97
00:05:23,414 --> 00:05:26,814
Those five letters didn't prove she was alive.

98
00:05:26,814 --> 00:05:32,414
Even so, they were the first thing that morning to make me want to reach the next one.

99
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:35,960
The receiver went dark.

100
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:38,060
The batteries had run out.

101
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:41,540
The employee pointed to a cable that led up to the roof.

102
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:46,180
The power came from a panel, but a connection had come loose.

103
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:51,420
If we left everything as it was, the warning would disappear, and someone might enter through

104
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:54,420
the very door we had just managed to bypass.

105
00:05:54,942 --> 00:05:58,542
As we were leaving, my radio bumped against a shelf.

106
00:05:58,542 --> 00:06:02,942
A tin can fell, clattering loudly against the concrete.

107
00:06:02,942 --> 00:06:05,942
The knocking behind the door ceased.

108
00:06:05,942 --> 00:06:09,942
Then came a slow pressure against the metal.

109
00:06:09,942 --> 00:06:12,942
We didn't wait for a third strike.

110
00:06:12,942 --> 00:06:17,942
We ran toward the service stairs while the police officer pulled the security gate shut behind us.

111
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:22,540
The staff member stumbled on the final flight of stairs.

112
00:06:22,540 --> 00:06:27,140
I had already reached the landing and could have kept going, but I turned back.

113
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:30,780
He tried to get up on his own, but his leg wouldn't cooperate.

114
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:33,500
I draped his arm over my shoulder.

115
00:06:33,500 --> 00:06:37,920
The officer followed, pushing the door until the latch clicked into place.

116
00:06:37,920 --> 00:06:39,510
We climbed together.

117
00:06:39,523 --> 00:06:40,550
One step at a time.

118
00:06:40,982 --> 00:06:45,302
Up on the roof, the city opened up before us.

119
00:06:45,302 --> 00:06:47,262
Smoke rose from buses,

120
00:06:47,262 --> 00:06:49,782
cars lay abandoned across the road.

121
00:06:49,782 --> 00:06:52,982
Groups of people fled between the buildings.

122
00:06:52,982 --> 00:06:55,942
On the avenue, a barricade gave way,

123
00:06:55,942 --> 00:06:56,392
scattering

124
00:06:56,392 --> 00:06:58,692
people across the street.

125
00:06:58,692 --> 00:07:01,732
A cable hung loose near the control panel.

126
00:07:01,732 --> 00:07:05,572
The staff member, sitting on the ground, gave us instructions.

127
00:07:05,572 --> 00:07:07,932
The officer held the flashlight.

128
00:07:07,932 --> 00:07:11,272
I reconnected the cable and waited for the small light to flicker back on.

129
00:07:11,802 --> 00:07:14,202
The radio crackled to life.

130
00:07:14,202 --> 00:07:16,602
First came a recorded announcement.

131
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:19,302
Then, a breath cut through the static.

132
00:07:19,302 --> 00:07:21,902
A voice asked if anyone was at the school.

133
00:07:21,902 --> 00:07:24,302
I pressed the button and said there were three of us.

134
00:07:24,302 --> 00:07:25,802
I didn't mention the mark.

135
00:07:25,802 --> 00:07:27,002
Not yet.

136
00:07:27,002 --> 00:07:29,658
On the other end, someone asked us to repeat our answer.

137
00:07:29,658 --> 00:07:31,558
I repeated it.

138
00:07:31,558 --> 00:07:35,578
The voice asked for three knocks on the handrail, a pause and then one more.

139
00:07:35,578 --> 00:07:37,078
We did as requested.

140
00:07:37,078 --> 00:07:38,718
They confirmed the sound.

141
00:07:38,718 --> 00:07:40,918
It was a conversation, at last.

142
00:07:40,918 --> 00:07:45,338
They said there was a shelter beyond the canal but that the main bridge was closed.

143
00:07:45,338 --> 00:07:48,118
Before explaining the route, he asked if we were capable of heading back through the

144
00:07:48,118 --> 00:07:48,793
building.

145
00:07:48,793 --> 00:07:50,653
"We went back to get the lady."

146
00:07:50,653 --> 00:07:52,633
I knocked twice, as promised.

147
00:07:52,633 --> 00:07:54,793
She opened the door, still holding the water.

148
00:07:54,793 --> 00:07:57,993
The staff member sat down near the window, and the police officer began sketching the

149
00:07:57,993 --> 00:07:59,833
route on a piece of paper.

150
00:07:59,833 --> 00:08:03,553
I didn't know if the shelter actually existed, but now we had someone who could hear our

151
00:08:03,553 --> 00:08:04,146
questions.

152
00:08:04,146 --> 00:08:07,666
The four of us set out, well away from the main bridge.

153
00:08:07,666 --> 00:08:10,266
The city remained in a state of collapse.

154
00:08:10,266 --> 00:08:12,266
Behind us a truck exploded.

155
00:08:12,266 --> 00:08:17,226
People were running along the bank, pursued amidst the wreckage, and my arm kept aching.

156
00:08:17,226 --> 00:08:20,466
Over the radio a voice guided us through smaller streets.

157
00:08:20,466 --> 00:08:24,826
When we reached the canal the voice stopped mid-sentence, the static grew louder.

158
00:08:24,826 --> 00:08:26,746
Then I heard my own name.

159
00:08:26,746 --> 00:08:28,792
In that voice I recognized Rosa.